Description: terminal network scanner and diagnostic tool
 netscanner is a terminal interface for surveying the network a machine is
 attached to: it sweeps a CIDR range for live hosts, resolves their vendor
 from the MAC prefix, scans ports, watches ARP and DHCP traffic, and plots
 per-host throughput.
 .
 It builds raw packets rather than shelling out to other tools, so it needs
 CAP_NET_RAW. Run it as root, or grant the capability to the binary with
 "setcap cap_net_raw+ep /usr/bin/netscanner". Without it netscanner exits
 immediately with "Unable to create datalink channel: Operation not permitted"
 rather than starting in a reduced mode.
